    "questionNumber": 46,
    "section": "SAT Practice 4 - May 22, 2026",
    "text": "Reading and Writing: Question 19Even though bats prefer very sweet nectar, the plants that attract them have evolved to produce nectar that is only moderately sweet. A recent study ______blank why: making sugar is energy-intensive, and it is more advantageous for plants to make a large amount of low-sugar nectar than a small amount of high-sugar nectar.Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?explainsexplaininghaving explainedto explain",
    "html": "<h3 class=\"cb-margin-bottom-16\">Reading and Writing: Question 19</h3><div class=\"cb-margin-bottom-16\"><p>Even though bats prefer very sweet nectar, the plants that attract them have evolved to produce nectar that is only moderately sweet. A recent study <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> why: making sugar is energy-intensive, and it is more advantageous for plants to make a large amount of low-sugar nectar than a small amount of high-sugar nectar.</p></div><div><p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p></div><ol type=\"A\" class=\"answer-options cb-margin-top-16\"><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>explains</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>explaining</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>having explained</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>to explain</p></div></li></ol>"
  },
