    "questionNumber": 51,
    "section": "SAT Practice 4 - May 22, 2026",
    "text": "Reading and Writing: Question 24Small, flat structures called spatulae are found at the tips of the hairs on a spider’s leg. These spatulae temporarily bond with the atoms of whatever they touch. ______blank spiders are able to cling to and climb almost any surface.Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?For instance,However,Similarly,As a result,",
    "html": "<h3 class=\"cb-margin-bottom-16\">Reading and Writing: Question 24</h3><div class=\"cb-margin-bottom-16\"><p>Small, flat structures called spatulae are found at the tips of the hairs on a spider’s leg. These spatulae temporarily bond with the atoms of whatever they touch. <span aria-hidden=\"true\">______</span><span class=\"sr-only\">blank</span> spiders are able to cling to and climb almost any surface.</p></div><div><p>Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?</p></div><ol type=\"A\" class=\"answer-options cb-margin-top-16\"><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>For instance,</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>However,</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>Similarly,</p></div></li><li class=\"\"><div class=\"\"><p>As a result,</p></div></li></ol>"
